top-level lets, patterns, extensions, and externals are exports: true
underscore-prefixed lets, patterns, and extensions are private by policy: true
the opposing unprefixed value remains a detected zero-reference export: true
derived and hand-written sexp_of converters are excluded from the census by policy: true
nested lets and nested-module derived values are not exports: true
a deriving on the last declaration covers its whole recursive type group: true
sexp derives the polymorphic-variant parser helper: true
every derived export-name set matches its complete PPX expansion: true
dune select alternatives are not mistaken for module sources: true
direct and nested qualified paths count outside the defining source: true
references in the defining source do not count: true
structure, chained, and local module aliases count: true
unqualified identifiers in an open scope count conservatively: true
comments and strings do not count as references: true
equal, compare, and of_sexp extensions reference derived values: true
a sexp_of extension references nothing: true
an extension does not credit a different derivation from the same type: true
a deriving references converters of its component types: true
an inherited row references its internal parser helper: true
the internal parser helper name matches the ppx_sexp_conv expansion: true
an inherited row in an extension also references its internal parser helper: true
opaque and ignored types do not credit unused derived values: true
a deriving attribute is not an ordinary opened value reference: true
a functor-application type path is accepted without guessed credit: true
include counts as a reference to every re-exported value: true
a synthetic zero-reference export is detected: true
a synthetic zero-reference derived export is detected: true
an export referenced only through an extension point is not reported dead: true
